    "result_text": "I've added PENDING claims, and all 4 tests in `bin/e2e` pass.\n\n**How it behaves now**\n- **Settling above the clerk limit:** when a clerk settles a claim whose due is over the limit, it goes to PENDING instead of being refused. The audit line is `CLAIM_PENDING`, carrying the claim's number but no `due=`. The check moved from `CheckClerkLimit` to a new step, `ApplyClerkLimit`, in `{action}.POST.yml`.\n- **Approve:** only a steward can approve, and never the claim's opener. The claim becomes SETTLED with its due frozen at its live figure at that moment, plus any late charge. The audit line is `CLAIM_APPROVED \u2026 due=<due>`.\n- **Reject:** only a steward can reject, and a reason is required. The claim goes back to OPEN and is bound again by the last statement if that statement included it. The audit line is `CLAIM_REJECTED \u2026 reason=<reason>`, followed by the rollup lines.\n- **Statements:** a PENDING claim keeps its statement binding stored, so `claim-stated` still shows \"yes\". The binding is ignored only while the claim is PENDING, through a new `Claim.isBound()` on the server and `isBound` on the screen.\n- **Everything else:** totals, overdue, the late charge, holds, statements and voiding treat PENDING the same as OPEN, using a new `ClaimStatus.isOpen()`. Only drafts can be edited, so PENDING claims can't be.\n\n**Stored data:** a new migration, `V22__claim_pending.java`, widens the status check on the claim table to allow PENDING. It finds the check the same way `V20` does.\n\n**Front end:** each claim row in `Claims.tsx` now has Approve and Reject buttons and a `claim-reject-reason` field. Totals, overdue and dues treat PENDING as open.\n\n**Decisions you may want to revisit:**\n- The request only said \"a steward\" approves or rejects; I made both steward-only. Only approving is blocked for the claim's opener, so an opener who is a steward can still reject.\n- The reject reason is sent as a `?reason=` query parameter rather than in the request body. A reason containing spaces is written to the audit line as typed, so it adds extra space-separated words to that line.",
